    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies that removing the first element yielded by a BoundedIterator also removes it from the underlying collection, and that iteration continues normally through the remaining bounded elements. <p>Setup: BoundedIterator with offset=1, max=5 over [\"a\",\"b\",\"c\",\"d\",\"e\",\"f\",\"g\"] so the visible window is [\"b\",\"c\",\"d\",\"e\",\"f\"]. After calling next() to get \"b\" and then remove(), \"b\" should be gone from the backing list, and the iterator should continue yielding \"c\",\"d\",\"e\",\"f\" before reporting hasNext()==false and throwing NoSuchElementException on a further next()."
